packaging/ — upstream packaging seeds
=====================================

This directory holds the per-package metadata that imud maintains upstream.
Since 1.5 a real debian/ directory exists in the repository root and builds
ten binary packages with debhelper (dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b; CI builds
arm64 packages for bookworm + trixie in debian containers, and the release
workflow attaches the .debs to GitHub releases — amd64 users build from
source). One subdirectory here per binary package:

  imud/            the daemon + imud-cal + imud-status (+ Python client)
  imud-utils/      network diagnostics: imud-mon (wire-pinned to the daemon)
  libimud/         client shared library (debian/ splits: libimud0 + libimud-dev)
  imud-signalk/    Signal K bridge
  imud-mqtt/       MQTT bridge (links libmosquitto)
  imud-influxdb/   InfluxDB bridge
  imud-mavlink/    MAVLink bridge
  imud-prometheus/ Prometheus exporter bridge
  imud-wmm-data/   World Magnetic Model coefficients (Architecture: all,
                   versioned by model epoch — the tzdata pattern)

The five bridges link libimud at runtime, so as .debs they
Depend: libimud0 (built from this same source).

Each subdirectory contains:

  copyright     DEP-5 machine-readable copyright
  changelog     release history in Debian changelog format
  description   synopsis + long description (mirrored in debian/control —
                keep the two in sync when editing)

`make install` / `make install-<name>` install copyright and changelog.gz
into /usr/share/doc/<pkg>/ so even a plain make install follows Debian doc
conventions; the debian/ build reuses exactly those files.

Notes for the future packager (Debian-archive submission)
----------------------------------------------------------

* The debian/ build is currently BINARY-ONLY (-b) for GitHub releases.
  Archive submission needs the source package: `make dist` produces the
  upstream tarball (imud-X.Y.tar.gz -> imud_X.Y.orig.tar.gz), format
  "3.0 (quilt)" is already set, and include/version.h must match
  debian/changelog at release time (see docs/RELEASING.md).
* Known lintian refinements deliberately deferred: /usr/lib multiarch
  triplet paths, changelog.Debian.gz naming (upstream changelogs are
  installed as changelog.gz by the Makefile).
* Build with the packaging paths:
      make PREFIX=/usr SVCDIR=/lib/systemd/system DESTDIR=<stage> install
  When DESTDIR is set, the install is a pure file copy: no useradd and no
  systemctl calls — user creation lives in debian/imud.postinst (the imud
  system user joins gpio and i2c; imud-mavlink's serial output additionally
  wants dialout) and unit handling in debhelper.
* systemd units are generated from etc/*.service.in with the real bin dir
  substituted for @BINDIR@; they land in $(SVCDIR).
* Configs in /etc/imud/ are installed non-clobbering by make; as .debs they
  are conffiles (dh handles /etc automatically).
* CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS from the environment (dpkg-buildflags) are
  respected; debian/rules uses dh_auto_* so hardening flags flow through.
* libimud's SONAME is libimud.so.0 and its data struct is append-only; only
  a (never planned lightly) breaking ABI change bumps the SONAME and the
  runtime package name (libimud0 -> libimud1). See docs/RELEASING.md.
* The upstream release tag convention is vX.Y (see docs/RELEASING.md); the
  Release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) drafts the GitHub
  release with .debs + tarball on tag push.
